{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OTODOR Snippet: Model Spec Seed  (the published spec sheet, per model)
  Part of the Specification Rendering Engine — see OTODOR-SPEC-ENGINE.md.
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose:   Supply a model's published specification values wherever the
             product's own `specs.*` metafields are not populated yet.

  WHY THIS IS IN THE THEME. The values below are the client's published
  spec sheet — the same canonical brand data as the specification list in
  otodor-spec-registry, which is also a built-in here. Keeping it in one
  snippet means every consumer (any collection template, any product page,
  assigned template or not) shows the same figures, instead of the sheet
  being pasted per template.

  IT IS STILL THE WEAKEST SOURCE. Consumers pass the result as
  `spec_default`, which the Value Resolver only reaches when the metafield
  is empty:

      product metafield  →  column seed  →  MODEL SEED  →  registry default  →  '—'

  So populating `specs.*` in admin silently overrides it, one product at a
  time, and this file is deleted when the last model is covered. Never
  read it in place of a metafield.

  Params:
    product   product object (its handle/title identify the model)
    title     fallback identifier when there is no product (manual column)
    id        registry spec id to look up (e.g. `door_thickness`)

  Model matching: handle and title are upper-cased and stripped of
  non-alphanumerics, then tested as PREFIXES, so `ZION+ Rose Gold` and
  `ZION+ Galaxy Black` both resolve to ZION+, and `SENTRY Pro` to SENTRY.
  A product no model matches (e.g. OHM) simply gets nothing.

  Echoes the value, or nothing.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # ── Identify the model ───────────────────────────────────────────────
  assign ident = product.handle | default: title | default: ''
  assign ident = ident | upcase | replace: '-', '' | replace: ' ', '' | replace: '+', '' | replace: '_', ''
  assign alt = product.title | default: title | default: ''
  assign alt = alt | upcase | replace: '-', '' | replace: ' ', '' | replace: '+', '' | replace: '_', ''

  assign model = ''
  assign keys = 'SENTRY,NEXUS,ONYX,ZION,ZEAL' | split: ','
  for k in keys
    assign klen = k | size
    assign head_a = ident | slice: 0, klen
    assign head_b = alt | slice: 0, klen
    if head_a == k or head_b == k
      assign model = k
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if model != blank and id != blank -%}
  {%- capture sheet -%}
    {%- case model -%}
      {%- when 'SENTRY' -%}
dimensions = 41.5 × 7 cm
bolts = 5 bolts
face_recognition = Yes (up to 20)
fingerprint = Yes (up to 100)
cards = Yes (up to 100)
door_thickness = 45–100 mm
backup_port = Type-C
battery = Yes (4200 mAh, 6 months backup)
weight = 4.4
deadbolt = Yes
two_way_talk = Yes
doorbell = Yes
inside_screen = Yes (4.5 in)
mini_screen = Yes
motorised_latch = Yes
      {%- when 'NEXUS' -%}
